<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">A checkout change touches four distant packages. A profiler also points to scattered reads in the image pipeline. Both suggest looking at what belongs together, but each has a different cost to measure.</p>

<!-- @before Staff Engineer Thinking :: staff -->
### Measure locality at the affected layer

For feature organization, trace a real change across files and owners. For a hot loop, measure the workload before changing the data layout. For Compose, locate the state read before moving it and verify the affected phase. A package move alone tells you nothing about CPU cache misses. [Compose read phases](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/phases).
